🚽 Test case: #193 -- a by-value struct member argument whose field type
🚽 doesn't match the parameter's struct type (`show(b.thing)` where `thing`
🚽 is a `gang Other` but `show` wants a `gang Point`) is rejected, the same
🚽 tag check that already guards a plain struct-variable argument.
gang Point {
    rizz x;
};
gang Other {
    rizz y;
};
gang Box {
    gang Other thing;
};

skibidi show(gang Point p) {
    yapping("%d", p.x);
}

skibidi main {
    gang Box b;
    b.thing.y = 1;
    show(b.thing);
}
